**Claim 1.** A food processor apparatus comprising:

a bowl configured to receive and contain food items to be processed, said bowl having an open upper end;

a lid removably engageable with the open upper end of said bowl, said lid having a central opening defined therethrough for permitting the introduction of food items into said bowl and for accommodating a processing implement;

a lower recessed surface formed in said lid and disposed adjacent to said central opening, said lower recessed surface being depressed relative to a surrounding portion of said lid so as to collect and direct liquids toward a discharge region; and

a flow guide integrally formed with or coupled to said lower recessed surface and extending outwardly therefrom, said flow guide being configured to channel and guide the pouring of liquids from said lower recessed surface in a controlled stream away from said bowl,

whereby liquids introduced into or collected upon said lid are directed by said lower recessed surface toward said flow guide and dispensed in a substantially controlled manner during pouring.

# Patent Claim

**Claim 1.** A food processing apparatus comprising:

a bowl defining an interior volume for receiving contents therein;

a lid configured to be removably disposed upon said bowl in a closed position so as to substantially enclose said interior volume;

a housing;

a motor disposed within said housing;

a working tool disposed within said interior volume of said bowl and operatively coupled to said motor, said motor being configured to impart rotational movement to said working tool;

said lid defining a single substantially circular central aperture extending therethrough and providing fluid communication with said interior volume; and

a contoured surface disposed adjacent said central aperture, said contoured surface being configured to direct a flow of liquid poured thereupon toward said central aperture.

---

**Optional dependent claims you might append:**

**Claim 2.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein said contoured surface comprises an inclined or funnel-shaped portion sloping downwardly toward said central aperture.

**Claim 3.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein said working tool comprises a blade assembly rotatable about a substantially vertical axis.

**Claim 4.** The apparatus of claim 1, wherein said housing is configured to selectively receive and support said bowl in a mounted position.

